---
title: Com Sign-In State Machine
---

%% Partially superseded by Identity Authority inversion.
%% sign/id is ceremony-only; acme/www commits session and token state.

%% Current runtime vocabulary. Future canonical lifecycle terminology is defined in
%% docs/security/idp-flow-lifecycle.md and is not implemented yet.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> PRIMARY_PENDING: start sign-in cycle

  PRIMARY_PENDING --> primary_route: primary credential accepted
  PRIMARY_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable primary failure

  state primary_route <<choice>>
  primary_route --> MFA_PENDING: MFA required
  primary_route --> SESSION_LIMIT_PENDING: session limit must resolve
  primary_route --> GUARDRAIL_PENDING: otherwise

  MFA_PENDING --> mfa_route: MFA accepted
  MFA_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable MFA failure

  state mfa_route <<choice>>
  mfa_route --> SESSION_LIMIT_PENDING: session limit must resolve
  mfa_route --> GUARDRAIL_PENDING: otherwise

  SESSION_LIMIT_PENDING --> GUARDRAIL_PENDING: session limit resolved
  SESSION_LIMIT_PENDING --> FAILED: session limit rejected

  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> CHECKPOINT_PENDING: guardrail cleared
  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> FAILED: guardrail blocks continuation

  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> checkpoint_route: checkpoint cleared
  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> FAILED: unrecoverable checkpoint failure

  state checkpoint_route <<choice>>
  checkpoint_route --> SELECTOR_PENDING: selector required
  checkpoint_route --> SESSION_ISSUANCE_PENDING: selector not required

  SELECTOR_PENDING --> SESSION_ISSUANCE_PENDING: activation selected
  SELECTOR_PENDING --> FAILED: selector rejected

  SESSION_ISSUANCE_PENDING --> COMPLETED: active session issued
  SESSION_ISSUANCE_PENDING --> FAILED: issuance failed

  PRIMARY_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  MFA_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  SESSION_LIMIT_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels
  SELECTOR_PENDING --> CANCELLED: user cancels

  PRIMARY_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  MFA_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  SESSION_LIMIT_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  GUARDRAIL_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  CHECKPOINT_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires
  SELECTOR_PENDING --> EXPIRED: cycle TTL expires

  note right of COMPLETED
    Welcome, return target, dashboard, and other
    post-auth navigation are route decisions after
    sign-in completion, not sign-in lifecycle states.
  end note

  note right of FAILED
    FAILED means unrecoverable, non-resumable cycle
    failure. Retryable credential or validation errors
    do not enter this terminal state.
  end note

  COMPLETED --> [*]
  EXPIRED --> [*]
  FAILED --> [*]
  CANCELLED --> [*]
